 about the  fact that you were in these  relationships that that made somebody  said to me is a big fan of your work  that that they felt that you had created  a song for every part of love you know  every almost scenario of Love whether  it's daughters whether it's you know  with your relationship yeah heartbreak  yeah do you think the fact you were  romantically linked had had anything to  do with your ability to tap into those  emotions it might have had  now that you mention it I've never  thought about that but of course  so many facets of life that I  experienced through  us being  socializing as couples yes  and within  agnet is in my marriage and all of that  of course that that inspired I'm sure  that inspired a lot of the lyrics  and and also one important thing is that  uh you know we  we lived in Sweden in Stockholm  and we were two couples  and it it made it very easy to be  disciplined in your work  um  there were you know if we had been a boy  band based in London or New York or L.A  there would have been so many  Temptations yeah  whereas we could be disciplined we could  you know go to work in the morning like  going to the office and write songs all  day treat it like a job yes  yeah and and that's why we were so  productive I think during those years  and we toured so little which is also  good because writing songs is not easy  when you're on tour  so I think that's a  that's one of the secrets behind why  we're sitting here today is that we  we could concentrate on writing so much  is there a song you wish you had written  that someone else's oh that's so so many  so many songs because you probably  listen differently to a lot of people as  well you know hearing what they've done  how they've done it no there's so many  good songs out there  you know my favorite pop song is  probably Ticket to Ride With The Beatles  is it yeah  but there's Hotel California and there's  Ava Maria and there's uh osolomeo  and Smoke Gets In Your Eyes so many  beautiful songs why what is it about  Ticket to Ride  I don't it's it's like a compact little  pop thing that is glittering and and has  the energy and  all the ingredients  maybe it's because I was such a beetle  fan as well yes and also I mean it's  what it goes back to what we're saying  right at the beginning which is you have  your own memories which is why you see  when fans cry when they come to this  concert this experience they'll be  bringing certain thoughts to those songs  that you do because that's what you  associate music yeah with and that's  that's the power of it  um and maybe that you know when I said  about being in the outer World they'll  have a connection point that just comes  comes through  um who are you listening to at the  moment I can't let you go without asking  you that is there someone  it's enough to be new it could be but  you know what phase are you in I am  actually  I haven't had a record player for  I think 40 years but I bought one the  other day a record player and a real  Hi-Fi system an old-fashioned system are  we talking like with vinyl or yes vinyl  yes  and I listened to  um Beethoven's seventh Symphony I was  the that was the last thing I put on  before I came here  so what have you been listening to your  music on until then through your phone  through your devices streaming okay I've  seen them headphones and and  other devices yes fine but how have you  found going back to vinyl all these  years on  because my partner said she wanted it  and I went to one of those shops where  they have it and you sit down in a sofa  and uh and and they play it back to you  Frank Sinatra and stuff like that and  it's  it I don't know it the sound is not  better but it but it there is something  with that something did they know who  you were in the shop oh yeah they did  how did that go down well they feel a  bit of pressure to make sure this went  well the guy was was you know one of  those nerds and he he had to tell me  everything about every speaker and every  player  so he was a bit nervous but he was fun  it was okay and because as I wonder you  you can go about your business without  people bothering you yeah I mean most  people  or many people recognize me but very few  people bother me okay but when they do  do they is it because they need to tell  you something about the song Thank You  For The Music that's it that's it you  did it you set it all up for me you know  it's been such a pleasure talking to you  thank you thank you very much thank you  so much and thank you to you for being  with us until we meet again take care  and goodbye  [Applause]  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

